# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Klasivo Cloud Functions — Environment Variables
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DO NOT put real values here — use Firebase Secrets instead.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Resend (Transactional Email) ────────────────────────────
# Set via:  firebase functions:secrets:set RESEND_API_KEY
# Format:   re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# Used by: emailWorker, sendContactForm

# ─── Sentry (Error Monitoring) ───────────────────────────────
# Set via:  firebase functions:secrets:set SENTRY_DSN
# Format:   https://xxxxx@xxxxx.ingest.sentry.io/xxxxx
#
# Used by: all Cloud Functions

# ─── App Check ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# App Check enforcement is INTENTIONALLY DISABLED on all callables.
# The Flutter client does NOT activate FirebaseAppCheck.
# Re-enable only after adding FirebaseAppCheck.instance.activate() in lib/main.dart.
# Phase 3 hardening item — NOT a launch blocker.

# ─── SENTRY_DSN — BLOCKER 1 STATUS ───────────────────────────
# SENTRY_DSN is declared as a secret on all 19 functions. If it is
# missing from Google Secret Manager, deploy fails with:
#   "Failed to validate secret versions: SENTRY_DSN"
#   "Build failed with status: EXPIRED"
# Resolution options:
#   Option B: `firebase functions:secrets:set SENTRY_DSN` (preferred)
#   Option C: hardcode the public DSN in src/config/sentry.ts and
#             strip 'SENTRY_DSN' from every function's secrets array.
# Until one of these is done, NO function-side code change reaches prod.

# ─── RBAC Functions ──────────────────────────────────────────
# assignRole, assignScope, syncClaims, changeUserPassword
# These functions use Firebase Admin SDK (auto-provisioned in
# Cloud Functions) — no additional secrets or env vars needed.

# ─── Runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Node.js 22 (firebase.json: runtime: "nodejs22")
# ALL functions (callable + Firestore/Auth triggers): Gen2
#   (firebase-functions/v2 onCall / onDocumentCreated / onUserDeleted / etc.)
# The stale top-level v1 functions/index.js + functions/services/*.js
# have been DELETED — they were a silent-deploy trap.
# Deploy entry point: functions/lib/index.js (compiled from src/ via tsc).
# firebase.json now includes a predeploy hook that runs `npm run build`
# automatically before `firebase deploy --only functions`.
